# Accepted Trivy findings for the Security Scan gate (.github/workflows/ci.yaml,
# job `security`; hardening plan H-0.5, 2026-10-18). That job and the contract
# test named below belong to the development repository's CI (noted
# 2026-11-07); a local `trivy fs --ignorefile .trivyignore .` reads this file too.
#
# The gate fails on fixed CRITICAL/HIGH vulnerabilities (scanners: vuln). Add
# an entry only for a finding that is accepted for now, never to make a red
# run green unread:
#
#   # <reason: why it does not apply or why the upgrade waits>; <who>, <date>
#   CVE-YYYY-NNNNN exp:YYYY-MM-DD
#
# One ID per line; the comment line directly above it carries the reason
# (tests/test_ci_workflow_contract.py enforces that). `exp:` makes Trivy
# report the finding again after that date.
#
# Empty on purpose: Trivy was not installed where the gate was written, so no
# finding was invented. The first red run lists the real ones (maintainer).
#
# Vulnerability IDs only. Secrets are not gated here (the SARIF report still
# lists them): a secret rule ID in this file would mute that rule for the
# whole repository, and a committed credential needs rotation, not an ignore
# line. A future secret gate gets path-scoped allow rules (trivy-secret.yaml).
